cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "reharness: a self-improving agent rewrites its own harness, not its model, and proves each change live"
abstract: "Bounded recursive self-improvement of an LLM agent's harness. When a repeated request comes back returned, a Revision Session reads the agent's own run, changes the Harness Package (tools, hooks, skills, prompts) and proves the change with a Live Probe on the same request; only an accepted probe is adopted, and only for that task. The session is never shown an answer. Measured on AutomationBench."
authors:
  - name: "The reharness Authors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/e13ven-arch/reharness"
url: "https://github.com/e13ven-arch/reharness"
license: MIT
version: 0.5.0
date-released: "2026-10-27"
keywords:
  - self-improving agents
  - recursive self-improvement
  - agent harness
  - harness engineering
  - LLM agents
  - continual learning
